y78q33Qv22/b509787818140f55903955f4ea996bbe/lettershoppe.jpg?w=640&h=640&q=50&bg=rgb%3A000000 640w","sizes":"(max-width: 1180px) 100vw, 1180px"}},"body":{"childMarkdownRemark":{"html":"<p>It seems like the cannabis plant as a whole gives us so many benefits that we are only just rediscovering. It’s believed that Cleopatra used naturally derived cannabis oil to keep her skin looking gorgeous. The 21st Century has seen increased demand for ingredients sourced from Mother Nature and cannabis fits right into that zeitgeist.</p>\n<h2>Cannabis and the body</h2>\n<p>Your skin is the largest organ of your body, but did you realise it’s also your body’s first line of defence against invasive toxins. The skin acts as a protective layer with the body’s highest density of cannabinoid receptors. Cannabinoid receptors sit on the cell surfaces, waiting for specific neurotransmitters (those found in cannabis) to bind them. Different types of receptors are found in other parts of the body, as well, in what is known as your endocannabinoid system (ECS).</p>\n<p>Cannabinoids are able to interact with these receptors triggering natural body processes that can reduce inflammation, calm anxiety, and soothe skin. Your body is always naturally producing cannabinoids that react with these receptors but they could always use a little boost from the outside. </p>\n<p>Cannabis holds the perfect ratio between omega 6 &#x26; omega 3 in hemp seed, a 3:1 balance which has a hydrating and plumping effect on the skin. Hemp oil also contains magnesium-rich chlorophyll. Chlorophyll is just what your skin needs during the winter thanks to its hydrating effects and ability to soothe itchy, red skin.\nEven though the hemp plant cannot have more than 0.3% THC to be legal there are still plenty of other cannabinoids in the plant that interact with your ECS system to support your wellbeing. Hemp seeds and oils can be consumed to improve your health and skincare from the inside out by providing the nutrients you ECS system needs to regulate your bodys balance. Also the more you keep your ECS system healthy the higher you can get off consuming THC.</p>\n<p>While much more research needs to be done, the existing anecdotal evidence and limited studies point to CBD’s positive healing potential. In a study published in the Journal of Clinical Investigation, researchers found that CBD can help reduce acne by curbing the production of sebum that leads to unwanted breakouts. Another promising cannabinoid study published in the Journal of Experimental Medicine found that CBD substantially reduced chronic inflammation.</p>\n<h2>New Zealand Hemp and Cannabis Based Skincare</h2>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/5JX5iZHLqWjdrcnnLfcAxs/dc24be40c8972139d5552da91a56bff6/Koaka_product-range.jpeg\" alt=\"koaka\"></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.koaka.co/\" title=\"Koaka\">Kōaka</a> harnesses the power of plants to create products that will refresh &#x26; nourish your skin naturally. Kōaka uses hemp grown in Canterbury, New Zealand as the base of all products. To get the oil from the hemp plant we simply extract the oil from the raw organic hemp seeds.\nWith its unique combination of active botanics, antioxidants and healthy fats hemp has rightly earned the title of 'the worlds most nutrient dense plant’.\nKōaka is giving the power and understanding of plant benefits back to the people.</p>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/6jevJZxzZwxnKS5I7jSvfA/f9883f78d1bb010fef59a5a31b29fc43/TOP_body_oil.webp\" alt=\"TOP body oil \"></p>\n<p>The Oil Project's <a href=\"https://www.tophemp.co.nz/hemp-skincare\" title=\"hemp seed body oil\">hemp seed body oil</a> includes key ingredients such as additional Vitamin E which is known to regenerate our skin cells at a rapid pace to ensure we keep on top of our healthy lifestyles.  </p>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/4uIStWKas6bsRomxlyk9JS/14ef594ada04af74cc4e1001d450b1c0/mato_hemp_wash_bar.jpeg\" alt=\"mato hemp wash bar\"></p>\n<p>Gentle on the skin, this luxurious botanical <a href=\"https://mato.co.nz/products/hemp-oil-manuka-honey-wash-bar\">wash bar</a> uses hemp seed oil extracts - linoleic and oleic acids, essentials which can't be produced by the body but can play a crucial role in skin health and anti-ageing. And while they moisturise and soothe your skin, manuka honey will leave you feeling cleansed, fresh and protected.\nWhen you choose <a href=\"https://mato.co.nz/\">MaTo</a> Hemp Wash Bars you'll be pleased to know that you are supporting a 100% New Zealand Made business. You can also rest assured that our bars are created with all-natural ingredients and compostable packaging. So go on, treat yourself - here's to making good choices.</p>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/66NXRuhxznjOkVxTCuzLmZ/df57c080706556d9c6627780ac8dbdba/hemp_health_bath_bombs.jpg\" alt=\"hemp health bath bombs\"></p>\n<p>These inexpensive <a href=\"https://www.healthyhempnz.co.nz/hemp-body-skincare\">Hemp Bath Bombs</a> will leave you feeling relaxed and refreshed. Containing organic baking soda, arrowroot powder, cream of tartar, epsom salt, hemp oil, distilled water and juniper essential oil. </p>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/724v4yP8xarXZZGoxGB1Hr/d7ff83a73d8ff53946d0d9bc9e280aa7/cannabisskincare.jpg\" alt=\"cannabis skin care\"></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.meccabeauty.co.nz/the-mecca-memo/the-in-tray/cannabis-sativa-seed-oil.html\">Mecca Beauty NZ </a> also sells plenty of beauty products that contain hemp seed oil. Often labelled as cannabis sativa seed oil these tend to mean the same thing. These products do not contain THC or CBD as these are still illegal in New Zealand. </p>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/4ASAmS7meVYqniZRZ86yVt/cc17844d08bdf491220b6aef63e6d6d1/hemp_and_kawakawa_cream.jpg\" alt=\"hemp and kawakawa cream\"></p>\n<p>KawaCreationz <a href=\"https://www.kawacreationz.net/product-page/hemp-and-kawa-kawa-cream-large-1\">kawakawa creams</a> are harvested following Tikanga and created in the heart of the Waikato. They are filled with natural qualities that help assist your skins healing process with conditions such as Eczema, dry skin, psoriasis, cuts, burns, grazes, rashes, sores, tattoo care, first aid. aches, pains and more..... Organic hempseed oil gives added nutrients that moisturises skin for longer and gives natural healing a boost!</p>\n<p><img src=\"//images.ctfassets.net/hqc28ezc40jg/1C01gntPMMQ641L2CgXlTi/19bfa7d6b8521e0f9c008d92574781a1/hemp_face_cloths.jpeg\" alt=\"hemp face cloths\"></p>\n<p>Amelia Skincare <a href=\"https://ameliaskincare.co.nz/collections/skin-care/products/hemp-face-cloth\">premium facecloths</a> are made from 45% Organically Grown Cotton &#x26; 55% Hemp Fibre. Hemp fibres have a natural resiliency to microbial growth is the natural choice for strength, softness and durability.\nThese facecloths are perfect for all skin types even sensitive skin.\nAs you enjoy the benefits of this natural pure product, you are also reducing the environmental impact. By growing hemp, we are cleaning up our polluted environment and helping to heal our damaged planet.</p>"}}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"cannabis-plant-skin-care"}},"staticQueryHashes":["3000541721"]}